<title>USA: BPA offers no surplus power again for Friday.</title>
<headline>BPA offers no surplus power again for Friday.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) did not offer any power for Friday, the fourth consecutive day the agency has refrained from surplus sales, BPA said Wednesday.</p>
<p>BPA said earlier in the week it was purchasing power to cover generation lost as several key reservoirs, including Grand Coulee in Washington, were being allowed to refill.</p>
<p>The lower discharge levels were expected to continue through Monday.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau, +1 213 955 6761))</p>
